# Keep the bundled Foam scaffolding out of release archives.
#
# `export-ignore` affects `git archive` only — that is, the source tarballs
# GitHub generates for a release, which are what Zenodo ingests. The working
# repository is untouched: the docs still render locally, the images still
# resolve, and nothing is deleted or rewritten.
#
# The rationale is the one stated in LICENSING.md: these three paths are the
# work of the Foam project under Foam's own MIT licence, not material of this
# repository. The Zenodo deposit describes "a git-native Foam vault of atomic,
# cross-linked Markdown notes", and shipping ~30 MB of third-party feature
# demonstrations inside a citable research artefact misdescribes it.
#
# Reversible by deleting these three lines.

assets/      export-ignore
_foam-docs/  export-ignore
_layouts/    export-ignore

# Normalise line endings so a vault edited across macOS, Windows and Linux
# does not churn diffs. Markdown is the canonical content here.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Treat these as binary: no line-ending translation, no attempted textual diff.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary

# The graph is generated, so never merge it textually.
#
# graph.json/.dot/.html are emitted by scripts/export_graph.py from the whole
# note set, and every node carries a degree count. Two clones that each add a
# note therefore produce different numbers on the same lines, and git reports a
# conflict on values that are both correct outputs of different inputs. Picking
# a side by hand is meaningless — the answer is to regenerate.
#
# `merge=ours` keeps the local copy instead of conflicting; the pre-commit hook
# then reruns export_graph.py so the committed graph matches the merged notes.
# Both halves are required: the attribute alone would preserve a stale graph.
#
# REQUIRES ONE-TIME CONFIG PER CLONE — `ours` is not a built-in merge driver:
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
# Without it this line silently does nothing and conflicts return. Set it
# alongside `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`.

graph/* merge=ours
